                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masaki+Kashiwara"} Masaki Kashiwara
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Riemann-Hilbert correspondence for holonomic D-modules
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.2374"} arxiv/1311.2374
          %blockquote
            %p
              The classical Riemann-Hilbert correspondence establishes an equivalence between the triangulated category of
              %em regular
              holonomic D-modules and that of constructible sheaves. In this paper, we prove a Riemann-Hilbert correspondence for holonomic D-modules which are not necessarily regular. The construction of our target category is based on the theory of ind-sheaves by Kashiwara-Schapira and influenced by Tamarkin’s work. Among the main ingredients of our proof is the description of the structure of flat meromorphic connections due to Mochizuki and Kedlaya.
          %p
            Generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+infinity-connections"} flat infinity-connections
            via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-nerve"} dg-nerve
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/iterated+integrals"} iterated integrals
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Block"}> Jonathan Block
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aaron+Smith"} Aaron Smith
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Riemann–Hilbert correspondence for infinity local systems
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0908.2843"} arXiv:0908.2843
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2013.11.001"} doi
          %p Another approach to higher Riemann-Hilbert
          %ul
            %li
              J. Chuang, J. Holstein, A. Lazarev,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Maurer-Cartan moduli and theorems of Riemann–Hilbert type
              %strong 29
              (2021) 685-728,
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10485-021-09631-3"} doi
          %p
            The relation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+Langlands+correspondence"} geometric Langlands correspondence
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Frenkel05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Frenkel"}> Edward Frenkel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lectures on the Langlands Program and Conformal Field Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %em Frontiers in number theory, physics, and geometry II
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0512172"} arXiv:hep-th/0512172
          %p
            An analogue in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+geometry"} p-adic geometry
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Riemann–Hilbert Correspondence in p-adic Geometry
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.hcm.uni-bonn.de/events/eventpages/felix-klein-lectures/fkl-2022-lurie/"} Felix Klein Lectures 2022
            %li#Bhatt21
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bhargav+Bhatt"}> Bhargav Bhatt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic geometry in mixed characteristic
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.12010"} 2112.12010
            %li#Mann22
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lucas+Mann"}> Lucas Mann
                ,
                %em A p-Adic 6-Functor Formalism in Rigid-Analytic Geometry
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.02022"}> arXiv:2206.02022
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Extension to the irregular case
          %ul
            %li
              %span.newWikiWord>
                Andrea D'Agnolo
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Andrea+D%27Agnolo"} ?
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masaki+Kashiwara"} Masaki Kashiwara
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the irregular Riemann-Hilbert correspondence
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.04260"} 2408.04260
